# The machines cabled together over Thunderbolt, and the address each one
# holds on its Thunderbolt Bridge. `mesh/build` turns every line into a
# `<name>-tb` host in mesh.conf and pins the address in mesh_known_hosts.
#
#   name     as in mesh/machines
#   address  fixed, on 192.168.2.0/24 — the subnet macOS Internet Sharing
#            hands out, and .1 is the box that would do the sharing
#
# The cable is a chain, not a switch: mac2019 — dorkyrobot1 — dorkyrobot2 —
# mini. Each Mac bridges its Thunderbolt ports, so the ends reach each other
# through the middle two, and a middle box that is off splits the chain.
#
# The address is not installed from here; it is set once on the machine:
#
#   networksetup -setmanual "Thunderbolt Bridge" <address> 255.255.255.0
#
# No router on purpose: this is a path between these machines, and a router
# here would offer the cable as a way out to the internet.

# name       address
dorkyrobot2  192.168.2.1
dorkyrobot1  192.168.2.11
mini         192.168.2.12
mac2019      192.168.2.19
